## FLOW MODE (`--flow` — Steps F1-F5)

## STEP F1: TRACE — Map the money chain
- [ ] Step F1.1: If topic provided → research money flow. Else → AskUser:
      Q1: "What TRANSACTION can you observe right now?" (actual money changing hands)
      Q2: "How many people are involved in this chain?" (who pays → who → who)
- [ ] Step F1.2: Trace minimum 5 nodes. For each: entity, $ per tx, volume/month, take_rate, monthly_income. Tag every number [K]/[T]/[?].
- [ ] Step F1.3: Calculate total chain volume (monthly $ flowing through entire chain)
- [ ] Step F1.4: GATE — chain volume < $10K/mo → WARN. All numbers [?] → BLOCK. < 3 nodes → BLOCK.

## STEP F2: GAP — Find position opportunities
- [ ] Step F2.1: For each node: who occupies it? Strength: STRONG / WEAK / EMPTY
- [ ] Step F2.2: For WEAK/EMPTY nodes → classify gap type: BROKER / REFERRAL / ARBITRAGE / AGGREGATOR / INTELLIGENCE / BUILDER
- [ ] Step F2.3: AI resistance test per gap: HIGH (trust/physical/license) / MEDIUM (human adds value) / LOW (pure info → skip)
- [ ] Step F2.4: Founder access test: can reach both sides of gap without capital?
- [ ] Step F2.5: GATE — all gaps = BUILDER → WARN, suggest pain mode. All gaps = LOW AI resistance → WARN. No $0 entry → WARN.
- [ ] Step F2.6: Rank gaps by (margin × volume × access × AI_resistance). Pick top 2-3.

## STEP F3: MARGIN — Calculate real income (KILL GATE)
- [ ] Step F3.1: Three scenarios per gap: FLOOR / BASE / CEILING. Decisions on FLOOR only.
- [ ] Step F3.2: Include ALL costs: founder hours × rate, tools, fees, communication, travel.
- [ ] Step F3.3: Calculate net_monthly = (volume × take_rate) - total_costs. Calculate $/hr equivalent.
- [ ] Step F3.4: Compound test: EXPONENTIAL / LINEAR / FLAT. Why?
- [ ] Step F3.5: KILL GATE — FLOOR < $200/mo after 90 days → NOT VIABLE, remove.
- [ ] Step F3.6: If ALL positions killed → KILL this flow chain, return to F1 with different transaction.

## STEP F4: ROLE — Match to founder + design entry
- [ ] Step F4.1: Founder-position fit: access to supply? access to demand? trust? language?
- [ ] Step F4.2: Entry design: Day 1 action, first transaction, scaling mechanism.
- [ ] Step F4.3: Disintermediation defense: what stops parties from cutting you out?
- [ ] Step F4.4: Pick ONE position. Save role.json.

## STEP F5: ACTION — 30-day execution plan
- [ ] Step F5.1: Generate scripts per role type (broker intro / referral pitch / arb buy+sell / etc.)
- [ ] Step F5.2: Week-by-week plan: W1=supply access, W2=demand access, W3=first transactions, W4=evaluate.
- [ ] Step F5.3: Kill criteria with dates: W2 <3 supply → kill. W3 zero deals → kill. W4 margin <50% floor → kill.

## FLOW MODE PERSIST
- [ ] Step F6.1: Save all outputs to data/hunts/HUNT-<date>-<topic_slug>/
- [ ] Step F6.2: hunt-meta.json with mode:"flow", position_type, status
- [ ] Step F6.3: Display full output. STOP. No chaining.

## FLOW MODE QUALITY CHECK
- [ ] Every $ amount has [K]/[T]/[?] tag?
- [ ] At least 5 chain nodes mapped?
- [ ] Position type is NOT BUILDER (unless explicitly warned)?
- [ ] FLOOR scenario used for all decisions (not BASE/CEILING)?
- [ ] Disintermediation defense designed for broker/referral/aggregator?
- [ ] Kill criteria have specific numbers + week deadlines?
- [ ] No Google "business model" searches anywhere?

