## ASYMMETRY MODE (`--asym` — Steps A0-A5)

## STEP A0: INTELLIGENCE CONTROLLER — Build verified money flow graph (PRE-STAGE)
- [ ] Step A0.1: Run IntelligenceController on founder's topic/industry (see hunt-lib/intelligence-controller-integration.md)
      - SEED: 3 targeted searches → initial graph (3-5 nodes)
      - HYPOTHESIS LOOP: generate hypotheses from gaps → test with targeted searches → update graph → judge completion (max 5 cycles, 15 web calls total)
      - High-value hypotheses: WebFetch FULL PAGE content (not snippets)
      - Low-value hypotheses: DDG snippet sufficient
- [ ] Step A0.2: Output `intelligence_context` with: verified entities, money flows with amounts, bottleneck positions, confirmed/killed hypotheses
- [ ] Step A0.3: Pass `intelligence_context` to ALL 6 scanners below. Scanners MUST check graph entities before searching for new ones.
- [ ] Step A0.4: FALLBACK — if controller fails (timeout/error), scanners proceed with independent discovery (current behavior)

## STEP A1: SCAN — Run 6 asymmetry scanners (with intelligence graph context)
- [ ] Step A1.1: Run founder-network-scanner (BLOCKING — interactive, asks 5 questions + money flow mapping)
- [ ] Step A1.2: Run 5 scanners IN PARALLEL using founder context from A1.1 + intelligence graph from A0:
      - money-flow-scanner (PRIMARY — SKIPS basic discovery if graph has flows, focuses on bottleneck scoring)
      - regulatory-scanner (uses graph entities to search specific compliance requirements)
      - cross-price-scanner (uses graph edges to identify price spreads between known actors)
      - cross-language-scanner (uses graph entities to check for partner programs)
      - timing-scanner (uses graph volume data to detect surge patterns)
- [ ] Step A1.3: Collect all signals. GATE — total < 3 signals → suggest pain/flow mode instead
- [ ] Step A1.4: Save raw_signals.json

## STEP A2: FILTER — Apply 6 asymmetry filters (KILL GATE)
- [ ] Step A2.0: Filter 0 — LEVERAGE TYPE (RUNS FIRST). Classify: ARBITRAGE(10)/BROKER(9)/INTELLIGENCE(8)/AGGREGATOR(7)/MEDIA(5)/WRAPPER(3)/BUILDER(1). Score < 5 = KILL. Kills all BUILDER and WRAPPER opportunities.
- [ ] Step A2.1: Filter 1 — Competition Density. COUNT competitors by name. > 20 = KILL signal.
- [ ] Step A2.2: Filter 2 — Protection Window. Months before copyable. < 2 months = KILL.
- [ ] Step A2.3: Filter 3 — AI Resistance. Score 1-10. < 2 = KILL.
- [ ] Step A2.4: Filter 4 — Founder Access. Requires > $500 to start = KILL.
- [ ] Step A2.5: Filter 5 — Margin After Competition. Net monthly ÷ (1+competitors). < $200 = KILL.
- [ ] Step A2.6: Calculate ASYMMETRY_SCORE = leverage(0.25) + competition(0.20) + protection(0.20) + ai_resistance(0.15) + access(0.10) + margin(0.10). GATE — 0 survivors → suggest alternatives.
- [ ] Step A2.7: Save filtered_signals.json

## STEP A3: SPECIFICS — Generate exact opportunity specs
- [ ] Step A3.1: For top 3 survivors, generate EXACT spec: POSITION [type] ACTION [connect/buy/sell/curate] SUPPLY [who] DEMAND [who] VIA [channel] AT [price] MARGIN [amount] COMPETITION [count] PROTECTION [months] SUPPLY_CONTACTS [5 names] DEMAND_CONTACTS [5 names]
- [ ] Step A3.2: Save opportunities.json

## STEP A4: VERIFY — Cross-check with real data
- [ ] Step A4.1: Customer existence check — find 10 actual people in target group (names/handles)
- [ ] Step A4.2: Price verification — search for comparable pricing
- [ ] Step A4.3: Competitor recount — search ONE MORE TIME with different terms
- [ ] Step A4.4: Forum complaint check — 3+ complaints with URLs about the problem
- [ ] Step A4.5: GATE — verification fails → downgrade or KILL opportunity
- [ ] Step A4.6: Save verification.json

## STEP A5: ACTION — Deal cards + outreach scripts + 14-day plan
- [ ] Step A5.1: Generate 3 outreach script variants (under 50 words each, tone matches position type)
- [ ] Step A5.2: Generate DEAL CARDS via deal-tracker.md: 5 supply-side cards + 5 demand-side cards. Each card: target name, channel, copy-paste script, expected response, deadline, margin per tx.
- [ ] Step A5.3: Generate 14-day action plan (Day 1-2: send supply + demand cards, Day 3-4: follow up + 10 more, Day 5-7: evaluate, Day 8-10: first transactions, Day 11-14: decide SCALE or PIVOT)
- [ ] Step A5.4: Set kill criteria with specific numbers + day deadlines
- [ ] Step A5.5: Save deal cards to data/deals/DEAL-<date>-<slug>/ and create ACTION file

## ASYMMETRY CHAIN MODES
- [ ] If `--asym --flow`: After A4, auto-feed #1 opportunity into F1 (flow tracer) → continue F2-F5
- [ ] If `--asym --pain`: After A4, auto-feed #1 opportunity into Step 1 (prey profiler) → continue 2-5

## ASYMMETRY PERSIST
- [ ] Step A6.1: Save all outputs to data/hunts/HUNT-<date>-asym-<focus_slug>/
- [ ] Step A6.2: hunt-meta.json with mode:"asymmetry", status, scanners_completed, signals_total, signals_survived
- [ ] Step A6.3: Save deal cards to data/deals/DEAL-<date>-<slug>/
- [ ] Step A6.4: Display full output. STOP (unless chain mode active).

